 "version": 1,
 "title": "Big Beat Groove",
 "category": "Drums and grooves",
 "text": "Sound: a fat, slow, dirty breakbeat that sounds sampled from an old record: a heavy kick, a big snare, eighth hats, all crushed and overdriven. The 90s big beat drum sound. It plays by itself.\n\nHow it's built: one Clock at 100. Kick from a Sequencer on eighths (steps 1, 6 and 7), snare on 3 and 7 with a longer, fuller decay, hats on every eighth. The whole mix through the Crusher (lower bits, half the sample rate: the old-sampler grit), then Drive, then a short Reverb.\n\nTweak: BITS and RATE, DRIVE, the kick steps, TEMPO (big beat sits between 95 and 115).",
